      "title": "Note: MOSS-Image",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MOSS-Image\n\nSettings from the MOSS prompting study: 20 steps, CFG 5, euler / sgm_uniform, SLG (uncond skip, layer 22, 0-1), empty negative, 1344x768. Prompt: prose, one sentence per element, no quality prefix.\n\nRTX 5070 Laptop: plain 22 s, Automatic (3 stages, \u0394 0.05) 18 s, Manual (0.5x to step 10) 14 s.\n\n## SPEED on an image model\n\nAll SPEED nodes here have **model_type = flow_image** and **noise_policy = coupled_full_grid**. The sampler input comes from KSamplerSelect (euler).\n\n1. **Harvest** (muted): unmute it, run once, and read the report. Paste `noise_amplitude` and\n   `noise_decay_exponent` into the Automatic node. The values already in it were harvested from this\n   prompt and seed on an RTX 5070 Laptop.\n2. **SPEED Automatic** (active): stage boundaries come from the Harvest fit and `Tolerance (Delta)`.\n   At \u0394 0.005 the low-resolution stage ends in the first steps, so it saves little; \u0394 0.05 is the\n   useful setting for images.\n3. **SPEED Manual** (muted): fixed boundary, half resolution to step 10, then full resolution.\n   Unmute it and mute Automatic to use it instead.\n\n`coupled_full_grid` draws the noise from the seed as SamplerCustomAdvanced does, so SPEED keeps a plain\nrun's composition at the same seed; small details such as an object count can still change.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## MOSS-Image\n\nSettings from the MOSS prompting study: 20 steps, CFG 5, euler / sgm_uniform, SLG (uncond skip, layer 22, 0-1), empty negative, 1344x768. Prompt: prose, one sentence per element, no quality prefix.\n\nRTX 5070 Laptop: plain 22 s, Automatic (3 stages, \u0394 0.05) 18 s, Manual (0.5x to step 10) 14 s.\n\n## SPEED on an image model\n\nAll SPEED nodes here have **model_type = flow_image** and **noise_policy = coupled_full_grid**. The sampler input comes from KSamplerSelect (euler).\n\n1. **Harvest** (muted): unmute it, run once, and read the report. Paste `noise_amplitude` and\n   `noise_decay_exponent` into the Automatic node. The values already in it were harvested from this\n   prompt and seed on an RTX 5070 Laptop.\n2. **SPEED Automatic** (active): stage boundaries come from the Harvest fit and `Tolerance (Delta)`.\n   At \u0394 0.005 the low-resolution stage ends in the first steps, so it saves little; \u0394 0.05 is the\n   useful setting for images.\n3. **SPEED Manual** (muted): fixed boundary, half resolution to step 10, then full resolution.\n   Unmute it and mute Automatic to use it instead.\n\n`coupled_full_grid` draws the noise from the seed as SamplerCustomAdvanced does, so SPEED keeps a plain\nrun's composition at the same seed; small details such as an object count can still change.\n"
      },
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    }
